2026-10-28T06:13:25.6276389Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6364789Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6373725Z [0m
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6374280Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6374870Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6375143Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6375482Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6376124Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6376493Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6376810Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6377291Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6377504Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6378321Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6378832Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6379203Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6379481Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6379613Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6379799Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6379993Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6380196Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6380488Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6380587Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6380843Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6380971Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6381261Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6381655Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6385108Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6385233Z I will:
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6385378Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6385611Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6386120Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6386652Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6387137Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6387458Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6387799Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6388301Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6388671Z    /root
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6398917Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6399431Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6409526Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6409959Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6410255Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6411627Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6412113Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6428098Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6428680Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6438029Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6438514Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6438973Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6439205Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6439412Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6439679Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6440007Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6440553Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6440950Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6441092Z If you would like to
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6441435Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6441655Z 
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6441900Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-28T06:13:25.6442330Z   $ sh ./install-nix
